statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, let U ⊆ ℝ^P, let R₁ = (C₁, θ₁, ξ₁) and R₂ = (C₂, θ₂, ξ₂) be integer multiplicity triples in U (IMRep U n, Simon Ch. 6, 3.1), and write Hⁿ = μHE[n]. Let:
- C ⊆ C₁ ∪ C₂ be Borel;
- θ : ℝ^P → ℕ be measurable with 0 < θ(x) ≤ 1_{C₁}(x)θ₁(x) + 1_{C₂}(x)θ₂(x) for x ∈ C;
- ξ : ℝ^P → Λ_n(ℝ^P) (MultiVector P n) be a.e. strongly measurable for Hⁿ⌞C.
Assume that for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ C ∩ C₁, ξ(x) = ±ξ₁(x) and every approximate tangent space of C₁ at x is an approximate tangent space of C at x. Assume also that for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ C ∖ C₁, ξ(x) = ±ξ₂(x) and every approximate tangent space of C₂ at x is an approximate tangent space of C at x. Then there is an integer multiplicity triple R in U (R : IMRep U n) with R.carrier = C, R.mult = θ and R.orient = ξ.
